================================================================================
                               APPENDIX A
                           ALGORITHM DETAILS
================================================================================

A.1 TASK ALLOCATION ALGORITHM
-----------------------------

ALGORITHM: Auction-Based Task Allocation

Input: Tasks T, Agents R, DSG G, Belief P(yG)
Output: Allocation A: T → R

1.  Initialize prices p_t = Priority(t) for all t ∈ T
2.  Initialize allocation A = ∅
3.  Initialize load Lᵢ = 0 for all rᵢ ∈ R
4.  WHILE unassigned tasks exist AND iterations < max_iter:
5.      FOR each agent rᵢ:
6.          LoadFactorᵢ ← exp(-β · Lᵢ)
7.          FOR each unassigned task t:
8.              Costᵢ(t) ← shortest path cost from xᵢ to t
9.              bᵢₜ ← (pₜ / (Costᵢ(t) + ε)) · LoadFactorᵢ
10.         END FOR
11.         tᵢ* ← argmax_t bᵢₜ
12.         Submit bid (i, tᵢ*, bᵢₜᵢ*)
13.     END FOR
14.     FOR each task t:
15.         Bidders(t) ← {i : tᵢ* = t}
16.         IF |Bidders(t)| = 1:
17.             i* ← single bidder
18.             A(t) ← rᵢ*
19.             Lᵢ* ← Lᵢ* + 1
20.         ELSE IF |Bidders(t)| > 1:
21.             i* ← argmax_{i ∈ Bidders(t)} bᵢₜ
22.             A(t) ← rᵢ*
23.             Lᵢ* ← Lᵢ* + 1
24.             Increase price: pₜ ← (1 + δ) · pₜ
25.         END IF
26.     END FOR
27. END WHILE
28. RETURN A

Properties:
  • Convergence in O(M log M) iterations for M tasks
  • ε-competitive with optimal allocation
  • Distributed execution with O(N) messages per round
  • Load balancing through exponential penalty

A.2 DISTRIBUTED CONSENSUS ALGORITHM
-----------------------------------

ALGORITHM: Distributed Belief Consensus

Input: Local belief Pᵢ, Confidence cᵢ, Neighbors Nᵢ
Output: Updated belief Pᵢ', Updated confidence cᵢ'

1.  Broadcast ⟨Pᵢ, cᵢ⟩ to all j ∈ Nᵢ
2.  Receive {(Pⱼ, cⱼ) : j ∈ Nᵢ}
3.  W ← cᵢ + Σⱼ∈Nᵢ cⱼ
4.  Pᵢ' ← (cᵢ · Pᵢ + Σⱼ∈Nᵢ cⱼ · Pⱼ) / W
5.  cᵢ' ← √(cᵢ² + Σⱼ∈Nᵢ cⱼ²)
6.  Normalize: Pᵢ' ← Pᵢ' / Σᵥ Pᵢ'(v)
7.  RETURN Pᵢ', cᵢ'


